 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? It' usually the light and camera angle that make it look like that. Use a soft light from behind and keep the angle of camera low and right of your nose. Use a full length shot from above and to the side, so you' not seeing your nose. That angle makes orange look at its worse. Shoot in the same room with the same light, but with different face shots poses. Pick the one you like the way it looks on its own, and use that for your thumbnail. Probably not. Mixing it up keeps your viewers engaged. A few bright close ups of your skin reacting go well too. Shoot in front of a window with a thin sheet of clear plastic between so it's soft rather than bright. Use flash only as fill so it doesn't look double lit.",
